      "writtenOn": "2016-07-30T20:29:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why does cutoff need to be int64 if only its lowest 32 bits are used?\n\nyou could define it as uint32_t and assign like\n\ncutOff \u003d (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)targetCnt * (1000000 - 1250) / 1000000));",
      "revId": "375da28a8b81b54e64cbe84209b8ffba7f6e746c",
